{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01R8SiNrnty4os4SiqJxi9M7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. **Q30 — Vocabulary mismatch (dense-only failing on keywords)** is written and committed.\n\n**What was covered:**\n- **Root cause:** Bi-encoders trained via contrastive learning optimise for semantic proximity. Rare tokens (SKUs, drug codes, legal citations, model numbers) are underrepresented in training data, so their embedding signal is diluted — semantically similar but not lexically identical docs outrank the exact match.\n- **Mechanism:** BM25's IDF weighting is complementary — rare tokens score *higher* in BM25 precisely because they're rare. Running both retrievers in parallel and fusing with RRF (Reciprocal Rank Fusion, k=60) captures both strengths. Elasticsearch 8.9+ and Qdrant 1.7+ support this natively.\n- **Fix stack:** Hybrid BM25+dense with RRF → cross-encoder reranking (Cohere Rerank / BGE-Reranker) → for fully structured IDs (SKUs), metadata pre-filter bypasses embeddings entirely.\n- **Concrete metric:** Recall@5 improved from 61% → 79% on identifier-heavy golden queries.\n- **Pitfalls called out:** Claiming \"a better embedding model fixes this,\" not quantifying the improvement, and assuming dense handles all retrieval needs.\n\n**5 items remaining:** Q31–Q34 + validate."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":385,"cache_read_input_tokens":60938,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":385,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2ab463a-3903-490f-8e33-24fcafc1a127","uuid":"853d6304-ec5e-400a-82b5-1f6978fd57f0"}
